action,x,y,origin,button,key,micros,note,platform
# P82 on Windows, GtkBackend: hover, hold and release the destructive buttons, the steps of
# actions/win/P82-destructive-press.actions (WinUI). GtkBackend draws a destructive Button as a red
# label on the ordinary bezel (2865c7d6); the label must stay red hovered, held and released.
# The last click is on the DISABLED one: it must not fire, so the final capture must read
# "pressed: destructive, borderless".
# Measured 2026-10-19 on a frame capture (window 508x528, scale 1.0, origin=frame): GTK's buttons
# are taller than WinUI's, and the WinUI positions put the borderless click in the gap between
# two buttons. Centres: bordered (117, 240), borderless (103, 276), disabled (114, 312).
# P82(Windows,GtkBackend):對危險按鈕滑過、按住、放開，紅字標籤不可消失;最後點停用的那顆不可觸發，
# 截圖須顯示 "pressed: destructive, borderless"。座標取自 frame 截圖(2026-10-19)。
sleep,,,,,,1500000,let P82 lay out,windows
hover,117,240,frame,,,,"destructive, bordered -- hovered; the label stays red",windows
sleep,,,,,,500000,let the hover visual settle,windows
mousedown,117,240,frame,left,,,"hold 'destructive, bordered' down; the label stays red over the pressed chrome",windows
sleep,,,,,,1000000,held,windows
mouseup,117,240,frame,left,,,"release; the label must read 'pressed: destructive, bordered'",windows
sleep,,,,,,500000,let the label update,windows
click,103,276,frame,left,,,"press 'destructive, borderless'; the label must change to it",windows
sleep,,,,,,500000,let the label update,windows
click,114,312,frame,left,,,"press 'destructive, disabled'; must NOT fire -- the label stays 'destructive, borderless'",windows
sleep,,,,,,4000000,hold for the capture,windows
